====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|fit}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fit]] (an [[arrow]]) against the [[bowstring]] of a [[bow]] or [[crossbow]].
#: {{syn|en|notch|pos=verb}}
#* {{RQ:Pyle Robin Hood|passage=Then taking up his own good stout bow and '''nocking''' an arrow with care, he shot with his very greatest skill.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cut a nock in (usually in an arrow's base or the tips of a bow).
#* {{RQ:Doyle White Company|passage=It is a Scotch bow, I see, for the upper nock is without and the lower within. By the black rood! it is a good piece of yew, well '''nocked''', well strung, well waxed, and very joyful to the feel.}}

